From 5d3f0781b14f642c45dfac435aaf5d2733868f19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] x86/k1om: MPSS instruction-set adjustments for the
 in-order MIC core

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6. The MIC core is x86-64 without SSE/MMX, without
port I/O, with an in-order pipeline and no fence instructions:
 - verify_cpu is skipped in the decompressor, in head_64.S and in the
   real-mode trampoline (it tests for SSE and reads IA32_MISC_ENABLE,
   which the core does not implement).
 - barrier.h: mb/rmb/wmb as lock addl; the TSC-deadline mfence in
   apic.c and weak_wrmsr_fence() are mb().
 - No port I/O on the card: the in/out helpers are stubs.
 - prefetch: ARCH_HAS_PREFETCH{,_DST} with the MIC prefetch forms; the
   prefetch/prefetchnta uses in copy_page and csum-copy are guarded.
 - MTRR: set_mtrr_state() returns the deferred state on MK1OM.
 - vmlinux.lds.S: the kernel image-size ASSERT is off for EARLYMIC.

Adaptations for 6.18: the raw in/out helpers moved to asm/shared/io.h
(6.0) and are stubbed there, asm/io.h keeps the _p/string forms in the
BUILDIO(bwl, type) shape; weak_wrmsr_fence() became an alternative in
processor.h (6.12); the TSC-deadline fence guard follows 4.4's apic.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
